# Third-Party Licenses

multimod is distributed under the **Apache License 2.0** (see `LICENSE.md`).

## Bundled in the package

### energyRt — `example_models$energyRt`

The `example_models` dataset bundles model source generated from energyRt's
BASE_UTOPIA scenario, in GAMS, GMPL and JuMP form, together with its parsed
multimod representation.

- **Source:** https://github.com/energyRt/energyRt
- **License:** Apache License 2.0
- **Copyright:** The energyRt Development Team

This content is derived from energyRt's model templates and remains under the
Apache License 2.0, the same license as multimod itself, so bundling it raises
no compatibility question. Full text: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

## Used by the documentation, not in the package

The website article "Two models from the field" reads the OSeMOSYS model
from a local clone of its repository (path in the environment variable
`MULTIMOD_OSEMOSYS_DIR`); the test `tests/testthat/test-read-gmpl.R` does the
same. Nothing of OSeMOSYS is bundled in the package.

- **Source:** https://github.com/OSeMOSYS/OSeMOSYS_GNU_MathProg
- **Files read:** `src/osemosys.txt`, `tests/utopia.txt`
- **License:** Apache License 2.0
- **Copyright:** [2010-2015] OSeMOSYS Forum steering committee — www.osemosys.org
- **Cite:** Howells et al. (2011), reference below.

## In the repository, not in the package

`drafts/` is excluded from the built package (`^drafts$` in `.Rbuildignore`).
It contains a snapshot of OSeMOSYS source for the parked OSeMOSYS workstream:

- **Source:** https://github.com/OSeMOSYS/OSeMOSYS_GNU_MathProg
- **Files:** `src/osemosys.txt`, `tests/utopia.txt` (in `drafts/data-raw/osemosys_source.RData`)
- **Version:** v1.0.1 (2021-05-21)
- **License:** Apache License 2.0
- **Copyright:** [2010-2015] OSeMOSYS Forum steering committee — www.osemosys.org

The upstream Apache copyright header is preserved verbatim in the snapshot; the
upstream repository contains no `NOTICE` file. Apache-2.0 is compatible with
multimod's own license.

If the OSeMOSYS workstream is revived, cite:

Howells, M., Rogner, H., Strachan, N., Heaps, C., Huntington, H., Kypreos, S.,
Hughes, A., Silveira, S., DeCarolis, J., Bazilian, M., & Roehrl, A. (2011).
OSeMOSYS: The Open Source Energy Modeling System: An introduction to its ethos,
structure and development. *Energy Policy*, 39(10), 5850-5870.
https://doi.org/10.1016/j.enpol.2011.06.033
